In-Reply-To: <cover.1792233517.git.claude@p7x.dev>
References: <cover.1792233517.git.claude@p7x.dev>
From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Subject: [PATCH v8 5/9] jails/instances/lab-mail: Let Pat archive and delete
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: vtzlyukynrpptqylrlsqzvwwoxvssqty
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:39:11 +0000

With the list held on lab-mail, Pat archives and deletes there, and
the sync carries his changes to Fastmail. His login needs a password,
or any client could log in as him and change the list.

- pat@p7x.dev joins imap-users, the ACL, and the static passdb's
  filter.
- check covers his entry in imap-users.
- README.org says where his password lives.
---
change-id: vtzlyukynrpptqylrlsqzvwwoxvssqty

 jails/instances/lab-mail/README.org           | 24 ++++++++++---------
 .../dist/usr/local/etc/dovecot/dovecot-acl    |  6 +++--
 .../dist/usr/local/etc/dovecot/dovecot.conf   |  2 +-
 .../dist/usr/local/libexec/lab-mail/check     |  1 +
 4 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/jails/instances/lab-mail/README.org b/jails/instances/lab-mail/README.org
index c069588e..d5133cbc 100644
--- a/jails/instances/lab-mail/README.org
+++ b/jails/instances/lab-mail/README.org
@@ -15,8 +15,9 @@ rules.
   so it cannot archive or delete a message, or mark one read for
   anyone else. An agent logs in as its own address, such as
   =claude@p7x.dev=.
-- One login may change the list: =mbsync=. It must give the password
-  in =imap-users=, and a wrong one fails. mbsync syncs with Fastmail.
+- Two logins may change the list: =pat@p7x.dev= and =mbsync=. Each
+  must give the password in =imap-users=, and a wrong one fails. Pat
+  archives and deletes, and mbsync syncs with Fastmail.
 - Dovecot's ACL enforces these rights, not file permissions. Dovecot's
   user can write the whole maildir, so a fault in =dovecot-acl= or in
   the passdbs of =dovecot.conf= would let every login change the list.
@@ -37,9 +38,9 @@ The Fastmail credentials never leave =/data/secrets=. Only the
 services that talk to Fastmail can read them, as members of the
 =mailcred= group.
 
-Dovecot is the only program that writes the list. Every change to it
-is a sync from Fastmail, and goes through Dovecot, as the user
-=vmail=.
+Dovecot is the only program that writes the list. Every change to it,
+a sync from Fastmail, or a move or deletion by Pat, goes through
+Dovecot, as the user =vmail=.
 
 ** sending
 #+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
@@ -121,12 +122,13 @@ mounts it.
   it, as members of the =mailcred= group.
 - =mbsync-imap= holds the password of mbsync's Dovecot login. Only
   mbsync reads it.
-- =imap-users= holds the login that may change the list, =mbsync=,
-  as =login:hash=. Only Dovecot's auth process, as the user
-  =dovecot=, reads it.
+- =imap-users= holds the logins that may change the list, one per
+  line as =login:hash=: =pat@p7x.dev= and =mbsync=. Only Dovecot's
+  auth process, as the user =dovecot=, reads it.
 
-lab-mail holds only the hash of each password in =imap-users=. Hash
-a password with Dovecot's doveadm, which prompts for it:
+Pat keeps the password for =pat@p7x.dev= on beastie, in pass(1).
+lab-mail holds only its hash. Hash each password with Dovecot's
+doveadm, which prompts for it:
 #+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
 doas jexec lab-mail doveadm pw -s BLF-CRYPT
 #+END_EXAMPLE
@@ -139,7 +141,7 @@ mkdir -p /jails/data/lab-mail/secrets
 cd /jails/data/lab-mail/secrets
 printf '%s\n' 'login@example.com' 'app-password' > mail-creds
 printf '%s\n' 'mbsync-password' > mbsync-imap
-printf '%s\n' 'mbsync:{BLF-CRYPT}...' > imap-users
+printf '%s\n' 'pat@p7x.dev:{BLF-CRYPT}...' 'mbsync:{BLF-CRYPT}...' > imap-users
 chown 0:0 .
 chmod 0711 .
 chown 0:15100 mail-creds
diff --git a/jails/instances/lab-mail/dist/usr/local/etc/dovecot/dovecot-acl b/jails/instances/lab-mail/dist/usr/local/etc/dovecot/dovecot-acl
index 84e287c2..e922add1 100644
--- a/jails/instances/lab-mail/dist/usr/local/etc/dovecot/dovecot-acl
+++ b/jails/instances/lab-mail/dist/usr/local/etc/dovecot/dovecot-acl
@@ -1,8 +1,10 @@
 # Who may do what to the list; see the rights section of spec.org.
 #
 # Every login shares one mail store, so each is its owner, and an owner
-# would otherwise have every right. Anyone may list and read. The login
-# in imap-users may also set flags, append, copy, move, and expunge.
+# would otherwise have every right. Anyone may list and read. The two
+# logins in imap-users may also set flags, append, copy, move, and
+# expunge.
 * owner lr
 * anyone lr
+* user=pat@p7x.dev lrwstie
 * user=mbsync lrwstie
diff --git a/jails/instances/lab-mail/dist/usr/local/etc/dovecot/dovecot.conf b/jails/instances/lab-mail/dist/usr/local/etc/dovecot/dovecot.conf
index 1bd41a16..ea622dc8 100644
--- a/jails/instances/lab-mail/dist/usr/local/etc/dovecot/dovecot.conf
+++ b/jails/instances/lab-mail/dist/usr/local/etc/dovecot/dovecot.conf
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ passdb {
 passdb {
   driver = static
   args = nopassword=y
-  username_filter = !mbsync
+  username_filter = !pat@p7x.dev !mbsync
 }
 
 # Every login is the same user, vmail, which owns the maildir. The
diff --git a/jails/instances/lab-mail/dist/usr/local/libexec/lab-mail/check b/jails/instances/lab-mail/dist/usr/local/libexec/lab-mail/check
index 9659c967..663cbe02 100755
--- a/jails/instances/lab-mail/dist/usr/local/libexec/lab-mail/check
+++ b/jails/instances/lab-mail/dist/usr/local/libexec/lab-mail/check
@@ -76,6 +76,7 @@ synced_recently() {
 check "${creds} exists" test -f ${creds}
 check "${creds} has the login on line 1" has_line 1
 check "${creds} has the password on line 2" has_line 2
+check "${users} has pat@p7x.dev" has_user pat@p7x.dev
 check "${users} has mbsync" has_user mbsync
 check "${mbpass} is not empty" test -s ${mbpass}
 check "smtprelay can read ${creds}" can_read smtprelay ${creds}
